# Blueman Engine Editor — UI Rewrite to Match Reference

## Summary

Rewrite the editor UI to achieve pixel-close visual fidelity with the reference image, which depicts a modern AAA game engine editor (Unreal Engine 5-inspired). The current implementation is functionally complete but has significant visual mismatches in layout proportions, typography, spacing, chrome styling, toolbar design, panel borders, and overall visual density.

---

## Reference Image Analysis

The reference shows a dark, professional editor with:

1. **Title bar**: Black, compact (~30px), engine title on left + window chrome buttons right
2. **Menu bar**: Integrated into title bar or immediately below it — `File | Edit | Create | Window | Tools | Build | Help` — with "ZeGFX Workspace" label far right
3. **Main toolbar**: Two-row chrome strip below menu bar:
   - **Row 1 (left)**: `Save`, `Undo`, `Redo` | `Import ▼` | `+ Add ▼` | vertical divider | `Select`, `Move`, `Stealth`, `Scale` tool buttons | `Snap (0.50)` | vertical divider | `▶ Play`, `Frame`, `Stop` buttons | `Build ▼`
   - **Row 1 (right)**: `⊕ Perspective ▼` | viewport mode buttons
4. **Content Browser** (left, ~20% width): Tabbed panel with "Content Browser ×" tab, toolbar strip (`+ Add | Import | Save All`), search bar, folder tree view below
5. **Viewport** (center): Full render viewport with in-viewport toolbar overlay (Perspective/quality dropdowns, Show ▼, transform tool buttons) + GPU stats HUD overlay + status pills (DR12, FPS, Frame, DRR, World Partition, Entities) at top right
6. **Outliner** (top-right, tabbed with "Save | World | Details" tab area): Search bar, 3-column table (Name, World, Panel) with tree view
7. **Details** (bottom-right, tabbed): Selected object header, component breadcrumb (`SkyAtmosphereComponent`), "Edit in C++" link, collapsible sections (Transition/Transform with XYZ drag fields, SkyAtmosphere properties), bottom tabs (Ray Tracing | Global Illumination)
8. **Output Log** (bottom-center): Tabbed (`Console | Logs | Programs | Profiler | Output`), toolbar (`⊕ Clear | ✓ Filter`), monospace log output with timestamps
9. **Render Control Strip**: Floating overlay panel on viewport with GPU info, quality presets, DXR/World Partition/Nanite/Isolation test controls
10. **Status bar** (bottom): Green dot status, FPS, CPU/VRAM, Tris/Draws/Entities, Selected info, Engine version, RTX quality, Level name, Git branch

